Let the HD-audio selector rename only the laptop's analog card ID, which Google's unchanged HAL
needs. Each laptop recipe labels its card's id path with gbos_builder_audio_id through
vendor_file_contexts and ueventd. Keep enforcing; no generic sysfs write access.
Drop together with the HD-audio selector.

--- a/etc/selinux/vendor_sepolicy.cil
+++ b/etc/selinux/vendor_sepolicy.cil
@@ -9275,3 +9275,11 @@
 (typeattributeset base_typeattr_244_202604 (and (domain) (not (dumpstate_202604 init_202604))))
 ;;* lme
 
+; Only the selected analog card's id is writable; never grant generic sysfs writes.
+(type gbos_builder_audio_id)
+(roletype object_r gbos_builder_audio_id)
+(typeattributeset fs_type (gbos_builder_audio_id))
+(typeattributeset sysfs_type (gbos_builder_audio_id))
+(allow get_variant_audio gbos_builder_audio_id (file (getattr open read write)))
+(allow gbos_builder_hardware_diag gbos_builder_audio_id (file (getattr open read)))
+(allow hal_audio_default gbos_builder_audio_id (file (getattr open read)))
